  "name": "Glioblastoma Multiforme",
  "alternateName": [
    "tcga_gbm"
  ],
  "description": "TCGA glioblastoma is the cohort on which most glioma computational biology was built, and 1,753 articles reference it in methods or results. Its imaging is its least-used asset: radiology exists for 607 of 617 cases and histopathology for 389, held in the Imaging Data Commons rather than the GDC, which is why most analyses treat it as a molecular-only cohort.\nIts follow-up is the fact most likely to trip up a new user. Median recorded follow-up is 12.0 months across 596 of 617 cases, reaching 127 months at the maximum - shorter than many users expect, because it reflects last recorded contact rather than total observation.",
  "url": "https://cancer-data-showcase.vercel.app/datasets/gdc-tcga-gbm",
